# Optional CLAUDE.md snippet

engram normally needs nothing in CLAUDE.md — context is injected by the
SessionStart hook. Add this snippet to a project's CLAUDE.md only if you want
Claude to actively curate the window during a session:

```markdown
## Project memory (engram)

This project uses engram (anchored sliding window memory).
- Prior context appears at session start under "Prior project context from engram".
  Trust it as the record of previous sessions.
- If we make a decision worth remembering beyond this session, you may store it
  immediately: `engram add --text "<one-paragraph decision record>"`.
- Never edit files under ~/.engram directly.
```
